<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Bakr Tihrani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Bakr Tihrani was a fifteenth-century Persian historian at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a>. Commissioned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a>, he wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitab-i-diyarbakriyya">Kitab-i Diyarbakriyya</a>, a chronicle of the Bayandur dynasty and its rise among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribes of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, which traces the rulers' descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oghuz-khan">Oghuz Khan</a> and is the main narrative source for the dynasty's early history.</p></div>
